15 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Nine bar graphs and two line graphs display OD600 measurements for two bacterial strains, Gv and E. coli, under control and light treatments at various time points. Two additional bar charts show colony counts by wavelength. Four rows of microscopy images compare live and dead bacteria for each strain under control and 415 nanometer treatment, followed by merged images. Two more bar graphs present the proportion of dead bacteria for each strain under both control and 415 nanometer conditions. Statistical significance is indicated on several graphs.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Panel A displays scanning electron micrographs comparing bacterial cell structure for Gv and E. coli under control versus 415 nanometer light, showing significant cellular damage after 415 nanometer exposure. Panel B contains bar graphs of optical density at 260 and 280 nanometers, with 415 nanometer-treated samples showing significant decreases for both bacteria. Panel C shows fluorescence intensity bar graphs, with higher values after 415 nanometer exposure. Panel D presents superoxide dismutase \(SOD\) and catalase \(CAT\) activity bar graphs, both reduced with 415 nanometer treatment. Panel E includes gel electrophoresis images and bar graphs, with pronounced DNA degradation in Gv but less so in E. coli after 415 nanometer treatment.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Bar graphs labeled A, B, and C on the left show statistical comparisons of cell viability and fluorescence intensity at different time points; fluorescence microscopy images on the right labeled \215Live,\216 \215Dead,\216 and \215Merge\216 display green-stained live cells and sparse red-stained dead cells in control, 10 minute, 20 minute, and 30 minute sample groups, with scale bars indicating 100 micrometers.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Panel A contains three diagrams with mouse images representing NC, AC, and Experimental groups, each illustrating timelines for estradiol injection, vaginal perfusion, LED/Me treatment, PBS, tissue collection, and vaginal lavage. Panel B features three bar charts labeled Chao1, Shannon, and Simpson representing microbial diversity indices for NC, BV, LED, and Me groups, with statistical markers for significance \(**, ns\).) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
